# - resource -------------------------------------------------------------------

<https://hl7.cz/terminology/ValueSet/personal-relationship-cz> a fhir:ValueSet ;
  fhir:nodeRole fhir:treeRoot ;
  fhir:Resource.id [ fhir:value "personal-relationship-cz"] ;
  fhir:Resource.language [ fhir:value "cs"] ;
  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "extensions" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xml:lang=\"cs\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" lang=\"cs\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: ValueSet personal-relationship-cz</b></p><a name=\"personal-relationship-cz\"> </a><a name=\"hcpersonal-relationship-cz\"> </a><div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #d9e0e7; padding: 6px; margin: 4px; border: 1px solid #8da1b4; border-radius: 5px; line-height: 60%\"><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px\">Language: cs</p></div><p>This ValueSet requires the Code system Supplement <a href=\"CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode-cz.html\">RoleCode (CZ Supplement)</a>.</p><ul><li>Include these codes as defined in <a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html\"><code>http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-RoleCode</code></a><span title=\"Version is explicitly stated to be 4.0.0\"> version ?4.0.0</span><table class=\"none\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-NOK\">NOK</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">next of kin</td><td>Played by an individual who is designated as the next of kin for another individual which scopes the role.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-FAMMEMB\">FAMMEMB</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">family member</td><td>A relationship between two people characterizing their \"familial\" relationship</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-FRND\">FRND</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">unrelated friend</td><td>The player of the role is a person who is known, liked, and trusted by the scoping person.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-NBOR\">NBOR</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">neighbor</td><td>The player of the role lives near or next to the scoping person.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-DAUFOST\">DAUFOST</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">foster daughter</td><td>The player of the role is a female child receiving parental care and nurture from the scoping person (parent) but not related to him or her through legal or blood ties.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-AUNT\">AUNT</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">aunt</td><td>The player of the role is a sister of the scoping person's mother or father.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-GRNDSON\">GRNDSON</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">grandson</td><td>The player of the role is a son of the scoping person's son or daughter.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-GRMTH\">GRMTH</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">grandmother</td><td>The player of the role is the mother of the scoping person's mother or father.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-DOMPART\">DOMPART</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">domestic partner</td><td>The player of the role cohabits with the scoping person but is not the scoping person's spouse.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-DAUADOPT\">DAUADOPT</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">adopted daughter</td><td>The player of the role is a female child taken into a family through legal means and raised by the scoping person (parent) as his or her own child.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-SONINLAW\">SONINLAW</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">son in-law</td><td>The player of the role is the husband of scoping person's daughter.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-NIENEPH\">NIENEPH</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">niece/nephew</td><td>The player of the role is a child of scoping person's brother or sister or of the brother or sister of the scoping person's spouse.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-UNCLE\">UNCLE</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">uncle</td><td>The player of the role is a brother of the scoping person's mother or father.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-GGRFTH\">GGRFTH</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">great grandfather</td><td>The player of the role is the father of the scoping person's grandparent.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-BROINLAW\">BROINLAW</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">brother-in-law</td><td>The player of the role is: (1) a brother of the scoping person's spouse, or (2) the husband of the scoping person's sister, or (3) the husband of a sister of the scoping person's spouse.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-CHLDFOST\">CHLDFOST</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">foster child</td><td>The player of the role is a child receiving parental care and nurture from the scoping person (parent) but not related to him or her through legal or blood ties.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-DAUC\">DAUC</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">daughter</td><td>**Description:** The player of the role is a female child (of any type) of scoping entity (parent)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-SONC\">SONC</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">son</td><td>**Description:** The player of the role is a male child (of any type) of scoping entity (parent)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-STPCHLD\">STPCHLD</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">step child</td><td>The player of the role is a child of the scoping person's spouse by a previous union.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-DAUINLAW\">DAUINLAW</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">daughter in-law</td><td>The player of the role is the wife of scoping person's son.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-COUSN\">COUSN</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">cousin</td><td>The player of the role is a relative of the scoping person descended from a common ancestor, such as a grandparent, by two or more steps in a diverging line.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-SON\">SON</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">natural son</td><td>The player of the role is a male offspring of the scoping entity (parent).</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-SPS\">SPS</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">spouse</td><td>The player of the role is a marriage partner of the scoping person.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-CHLDADOPT\">CHLDADOPT</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">adopted child</td><td>The player of the role is a child taken into a family through legal means and raised by the scoping person (parent) as his or her own child.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-NCHILD\">NCHILD</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">natural child</td><td>The player of the role is an offspring of the scoping entity as determined by birth.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-SIGOTHR\">SIGOTHR</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">significant other</td><td>A person who is important to one's well being; especially a spouse or one in a similar relationship. (The player is the one who is important)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-GGRMTH\">GGRMTH</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">great grandmother</td><td>The player of the role is the mother of the scoping person's grandparent.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-MTH\">MTH</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">mother</td><td>The player of the role is a female who conceives, gives birth to, or raises and nurtures the scoping entity (child).</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-MTHINLAW\">MTHINLAW</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">mother-in-law</td><td>The player of the role is the mother of the scoping person's husband or wife.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-BRO\">BRO</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">brother</td><td>The player of the role is a male sharing one or both parents in common with the scoping entity.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-HUSB\">HUSB</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">husband</td><td>The player of the role is a man joined to a woman (scoping person) in marriage.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-PRN\">PRN</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">parent</td><td>The player of the role is one who begets, gives birth to, or nurtures and raises the scoping entity (child).</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-SIB\">SIB</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">sibling</td><td>The player of the role shares one or both parents in common with the scoping entity.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-NIECE\">NIECE</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">niece</td><td>The player of the role is a daughter of the scoping person's brother or sister or of the brother or sister of the scoping person's spouse.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-FTH\">FTH</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">father</td><td>The player of the role is a male who begets or raises or nurtures the scoping entity (child).</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-FTHINLAW\">FTHINLAW</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">father-in-law</td><td>The player of the role is the father of the scoping person's husband or wife.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-STPSON\">STPSON</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">stepson</td><td>The player of the role is a son of the scoping person's spouse by a previous union.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-SONFOST\">SONFOST</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">foster son</td><td>The player of the role is a male child receiving parental care and nurture from the scoping person (parent) but not related to him or her through legal or blood ties.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-GGRPRN\">GGRPRN</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">great grandparent</td><td>The player of the role is a parent of the scoping person's grandparent.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-GRNDCHILD\">GRNDCHILD</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">grandchild</td><td>The player of the role is a child of the scoping person's son or daughter.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-EXT\">EXT</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">extended family member</td><td>**Description:** A family member not having an immediate genetic or legal relationship e.g. Aunt, cousin, great grandparent, grandchild, grandparent, niece, nephew or uncle.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-SISINLAW\">SISINLAW</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">sister-in-law</td><td>The player of the role is: (1) a sister of the scoping person's spouse, or (2) the wife of the scoping person's brother, or (3) the wife of a brother of the scoping person's spouse.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-WIFE\">WIFE</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">wife</td><td>The player of the role is a woman joined to a man (scoping person) in marriage.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-DAU\">DAU</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">natural daughter</td><td>The player of the role is a female offspring of the scoping entity (parent).</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-GRPRN\">GRPRN</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">grandparent</td><td>The player of the role is a parent of the scoping person's mother or father.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-CHILD\">CHILD</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">child</td><td>The player of the role is a child of the scoping entity.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-GRNDDAU\">GRNDDAU</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">granddaughter</td><td>The player of the role is a daughter of the scoping person's son or daughter.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-GRFTH\">GRFTH</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">grandfather</td><td>The player of the role is the father of the scoping person's mother or father.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-PRNINLAW\">PRNINLAW</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">parent in-law</td><td>The player of the role is the parent of scoping person's husband or wife.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-ROOM\">ROOM</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">Roommate</td><td>One who shares living quarters with the subject.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-CHLDINLAW\">CHLDINLAW</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">child-in-law</td><td>The player of the role is the spouse of scoping person's child.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-SONADOPT\">SONADOPT</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">adopted son</td><td>The player of the role is a male child taken into a family through legal means and raised by the scoping person (parent) as his or her own child.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-STPDAU\">STPDAU</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">stepdaughter</td><td>The player of the role is a daughter of the scoping person's spouse by a previous union.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-NEPHEW\">NEPHEW</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">nephew</td><td>The player of the role is a son of the scoping person's brother or sister or of the brother or sister of the scoping person's spouse.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://terminology.hl7.org/7.3.0/CodeSystem-v3-RoleCode.html#v3-RoleCode-SIS\">SIS</a></td><td style=\"color: #cccccc\">sister</td><td>The player of the role is a female sharing one or both parents in common with the scoping entity.</td></tr></table></li></ul></div>"
  ] ;
